<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Localiser Related Problems</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">There are a number of localiser related problems, which often can be easily resolved.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">Localiser error: Initialisation</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">"</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Localiser error: initialisation</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">" appears in sensor view when the localiser seems to be correctly connected.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Solution</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check the localiser settings are correct.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="bullet">&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">Wrong FARO BIOS version</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">KUBE will only scan correctly with the following BIOS versions:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">BIOS 7.20 - FARO Gold localiser (front option port only).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">BIOS 7.31/7.61 - FARO Gold localiser (front and rear option port).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">BIOS 4.82 - FARO Silver localiser.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">BIOS 7.20 - FARO Sterling localiser.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">BIOS 3.3.0.16, 3.3.0.32, 5.0.2.6, 5.0.9.3 - FARO Platinum/Titanium localiser.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If you are using incorrect FARO BIOS version KUBE will display an error message.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="color:#000000; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP171697186" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If you are using FARO Gold (front port) localiser with wrong BIOS version, the following error message will appear:</span></p>
<p class="Normal"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image002.gif" width="403px" height="126px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">To update your BIOS:</span></b></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Connect and power up the localiser as normal.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Run the relevant executable for your localiser type. (Sometimes connection to the localiser fails if you are not using COM1. In this case reconfigure your system so you can use COM1 and try again).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Please e-mail the localiser serial number (the serial number is on the base of the localiser) to FARO support informing them of the new BIOS version.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">No Localiser connection</span></h2>
<p><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">For all localisers</span></b></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">First check the baud rate. If the localiser has been reset it will need to be changed to 115200.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check that no other software that uses the serial port is running on the PC. (For instance you can not have both KUBE and Caliper 3D running at the same time.)</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check that all power and data connections to localiser are secure.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check localiser type and communications are correctly selected in software.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">For CimCore</span></b></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Please refer to manufacturers instructions.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">Not usable</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image003.gif" width="403px" height="126px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Ensure that the correct localiser type is selected in software.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">If correct localiser type is selected then contact your supplier for a new password. Send a request e-mail/fax containing:</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The Dongle Serial Number printed on dongle.</p>
<p>The Dongle ID as displayed in password dialog.</p>
<p class="Normal">&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">FARO Localiser not responding</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img id="_x0000_i1039" src="../images/slvr_led.gif" width="150px" height="148px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Possible reason:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">The six transducer numbered LEDs are illuminated when the controller box power is turned on.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Solution</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: In a systematic manner, the user must rotate links 1 through 7 until the lights on the front of the controller box turn off. This takes the incremental encoders through their reference positions.</span></p>
<p class="Warning" id="P1"><span lang="EN-GB">The FARO localiser will not operate until all red LEDs are off.&#160;</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Run Caliper 3D.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Select menu option Digitize/Setup.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check that Locked Plane is set to XY rather than USER.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image004.gif" width="512px" height="380px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">FARO Localiser beeps during scanning</span></h2>
<p><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Possible reasons:</span></b></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">One reason is that the one or more of the joints may have reached their limits.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">This may also occur if you have the trigger option installed. Apart from being irritating, the beeps will also badly affect the data quality since they cause delays in the FARO control box.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Solution</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Start scanning and then remove the trigger cable from the FARO localiser. The beeps should stop.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">To turn off the beeps, exit KUBE and run the FARO utility program, Caliper 3D.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">From the Settings menu select Configuration. Make sure the Controller Beeps check box is cleared. Ensure that Units is set to mm for use with KUBE.<br>
<img src="../images/image005.gif" width="263px" height="316px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Exit Caliper, replace the trigger cable and restart KUBE.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="bullet">&#160;</p>
<h2>Adaptive Laser Power and FARO Gold/Silver/Sterling Localiser</h2>
<p>If you use FARO Gold/Silver/Sterling localiser it is recommended to switch off the option Adaptive laser power. Currently there appear some problems when using this combination:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the laser blinks.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the scanned patches are not smooth  a lot of stripes are not captured.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="whs8">Solution: <span style="font-weight:normal;">Is you need to change the laser power while scanning a complex surface, then:</span></p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Use profiles:</p>
</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">make profiles for the different surfaces (coloured, shiny, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">switch between profiles when scanning the object.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ol start="2" type="1" class="whs9">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Use Autoset laser power when scanning different parts of the object.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="steps">&#160;</p>
<h2>FARO USB Localiser</h2>
<p>If you have one of the following issues:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Each second or third stripe is missing during scanning.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">During alignment stripe RMS values are much higher than normal (hundreds of microns).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">With KUBE running and laser turned on, but not in Scan or Pause mode, after a while localiser coordinates stop updating.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">If there are wavy patches.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Solution:</b></span> <span style="margin-left:0px;">Set screw in last joint of the localiser is not tightened properly.</span></p>
